{
  "passage": "Mrs. Brown, a 68-year-old retired housewife, had always been hopeful about traveling. Her grandchild, who lives in Canada, invited her for a visit. After saving for years, Mrs. Brown applied for a passport. The application took a long time, but she didn't give up. Finally, the day came when she could fly. Before leaving, she used an answerphone to leave a message for her son, ensuring him she was fine. The flight was exciting, and upon landing, her grandchild greeted her with a warm hug. They drove to a countryside area where a gentle stream flowed through the forest. Walking by the stream, Mrs. Brown shared stories from her youth. She felt it was important to give credit to her late husband, who had always supported her dreams. Later, her grandchild helped her set up a small exhibition of old family photos in the local community centre. It was a joyful reunion full of new memories.",
